# To increase the potency of an [[alcohol]]ic beverage similarly to [[distillation]] by chilling it to below the freezing point of water, removing the water ice crystals that form, and leaving the still-liquid alcoholic portion.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1941|journal=Esquire|volume=15|issue=1-3|page=176
|passage=Fruit of the orchard has been "'''jacked'''" these many generations, with Plymouth Rockers putting the hard cider barrel down into the ground to freeze, and {{...}}}}
